@startuml
'=============================================================================
' KIND      MEASURED -- every class, attribute and relationship below was
'           read out of the source or out of a real record on disk.
' GROUNDING taskmodel/task_model.py (Problem, Source, TaskModel, Report,
'           TaskType); fleet/fleet.py (Worker dataclass and its properties,
'           establish/record_run/promote); fleet/inbox.py (ledger entries,
'           TERMINAL, IDENTITY_POLICIES, retained_name); fleet/input_set.py;
'           and the on-disk records under fleet/workers/acme-august-recon/
'           (worker.json, versions/v1.json, input_contracts/v1.json,
'           history.jsonl) and fleet/workers/acme-timesheets/runs.jsonl.
'
' This is the domain model of ESTABLISHED WORK. It is drawn as a UML class
' diagram rather than an ERD because the durable state is JSON/JSONL files
' under fleet/workers/, not relational tables -- see
' docs/architecture/modelling-guide.md §2.
'=============================================================================
!theme plain
title Learning Lab — domain model of established work (MEASURED)

class Worker {
  .. identity: worker.json ..
  name : str
  purpose : str
  task : str
  base : path
  trigger : path
  customer : str
  input_adapter : str
  work_item_identity : str
  source_roles : map<role, RoleSpec>
  destination : dict?
  --
  engine : derived from task
  effect : model.on_accept
  committing : effect AND a committing runtime exists
}

note right of Worker
`destination` says where a result is
INTENDED to go. It is not permission to
put it there -- `committing` is the
separate fact. (fleet/fleet.py)
end note

class RoleSpec {
  label : str
  slot : "sole" | "shared"
  required : bool
}

class WorkerVersion {
  version : int
  model : TaskModel
  digest : sha256
}

class HistoryEvent {
  version : int
  at : timestamp
  event : "established" | "promoted" | ...
  digest : sha256
  why : str
}

class InputContract {
  version : int
  roles : map<role, {sheet, collection, header_row}>
}

note right of InputContract
Version-bound. A contract belongs to one
worker version; it is not a global schema.
end note

class TaskModel {
  model_version : int
  model_id : str
  task : str
  sources : map<name, Source>
  body : dict
  malformed_sources : str?
}

class Source {
  name : str
  path : str
  collection : str
}

class TaskType {
  name : str
  refusals : tuple<str>
  body_problem_codes : tuple<str>
  validate_body(model, base)
}

class Problem {
  code : str
  where : str
  detail : str
}

class Run {
  at : timestamp
  version : int
  ok : bool
  rows : int
  refused : int
  refusals : list<str>
  problems : list<Problem>
  run_input : {fingerprint, ...}?
}

class InboxItem {
  item_id : content digest
  file : str
  state : see 07-inbox-item-state
  precondition : {committing, effect_target_present}?
}

class Investigation {
  packet : dict
  question : str?
}

Worker "1" *-- "1..*" WorkerVersion : versions/vN.json
Worker "1" *-- "0..*" HistoryEvent : history.jsonl
Worker "1" *-- "0..*" InputContract : input_contracts/vN.json
Worker "1" *-- "0..*" Run : runs.jsonl
Worker "1" *-- "0..*" InboxItem : inbox/ -> processed/ | exceptions/
Worker "1" o-- "0..1" Investigation
Worker "1" *-- "1..*" RoleSpec : source_roles

WorkerVersion "1" --> "1" TaskModel : the established model
InputContract "1" ..> "1" WorkerVersion : bound to
TaskModel "1" *-- "1..*" Source
TaskModel "1" ..> "1" TaskType : task name resolves\nin the registry
TaskType ..> Problem : validate_body returns
Run "0..*" --> "1" WorkerVersion : ran which version
Run ..> Problem : records

note as N1
**The invariants this shape carries**

* A run names the **version** it ran, so a promotion never rewrites
  what an earlier run meant.
* `digest` is recorded per version in `history.jsonl`, so a version's
  identity is checkable rather than asserted.
* `work_item_identity` has exactly one implemented policy,
  `content_digest`. A worker declaring anything else is refused --
  it is not a default (fleet/inbox.py IDENTITY_POLICIES).
* `body` is opaque to `taskmodel`, by design: the envelope is shared,
  the task-family body is not. This is the same envelope-over-body
  discipline the Work Definition v0 contract reuses.
end note
@enduml
